docs/backend-perf/audit-terminal.md:- Mechanism: On macOS, `cmd_terminal_get_cwd` resolves the current working directory of the terminal shell process by spawning `/usr/sbin/lsof -a -p <pid> -d cwd -Fn` via `std::process::Command`. Spawning a child process and running `lsof` inspects system-wide kernel descriptor tables and takes 20–100ms per call. When UI components query terminal CWD (e.g. on prompt changes, tab switching, or split navigation), this induces high latency and consumes CPU spawning transient processes.
docs/backend-perf/PRIORITIZED.md:- **F-terminal-04 (Medium)** — `src-tauri/src/ipc/terminal.rs`: macOS `/usr/sbin/lsof` subprocess execution in `cmd_terminal_get_cwd`. Deferred because terminal CWD lookup is queried only on explicit prompt/tab events and is non-blocking to terminal streaming throughput; replacing with `libproc` requires FFI bindings.
